  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="ce344af3-e2fc-47e5-89a0-723db7a50b6f"><problem><para>
      <para>For the expressions in questions 1 – 4, choose which number would make the expression a perfect square. Then, choose an equivalent expression in factored form.</para>
      <para>\(x^2+3x\)</para>
      <para>What number can be added to make \(x^2+3x\) a perfect square?</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(\frac23\)</para><para>\(\frac49\)</para><para>\(\frac94\)</para><para>\(-\frac23\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(\frac94\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is: \(\frac94\).
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
